<h2 id="ha-ctrl-006-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Check every lock transition the integration supports, and the jammed, unknown and unavailable states. Unlock must not become Open unless the source reports it.
2. In a test installation, use an account without permission and an invalid code. Home Assistant must reject the request whether or not the control is visible. Never use real secrets.
3. Test Stop during movement, a cover or valve with no Stop, a partial position and a delayed confirmation. Dismissing a message must not claim the movement was cancelled.
4. Check keyboard review, return of focus, shared-screen privacy and long object names. Do not operate a real lock or valve just to test a colour or layout.

Record the Home Assistant and integration versions, the browser, the fixture or device, the starting state, the expected and observed results, and where the evidence is kept. A documentation check is not a live-device test.

For the request, pending and failed states see [Action requests and results](action-results.html). For wording see [States, requests and errors](../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html).

